evada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Justin Lee Brown | President CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $791K ranks in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Southwest Gas Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $6.6B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -27% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $252M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Utilities peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Price sits 20% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.20004348304381797},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Southwest Gas (NYSE:SWX) Stock Rating Raised to Strong-Buy at Wolfe Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/southwest-gas-nyseswx-stock-rating-raised-to-strong-buy-at-wolfe-research.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970913.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Everyone Is Watching Southwest Gas Holdings (SWX) Today","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-swx/southwest-gas-holdings/news/why-everyone-is-watching-southwest-gas-holdings-swx-today","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793928631.618,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.973,"tier":0,"scope